Abstraction:
Abstraction menas showing only the essesntial features and hiding the internal implementation details.
In simple words Displaying the things which are required and hiding the things which are not required.

How abstraction achieved in java?
Using abstract class
using interface

Concrete method: A method which has method body and it contains implementation logic.
Concrete class: A  concrete class is a normal class that is not declard using the abstract keyword, has complete method implementations, and allows object creation.

Abstract method: A method whihc dos not have method body.

Abstract class: a abstract class is a class that cannot be instantisted and my contain abstract methods.

IF any class inherits abstract method then that inherited class must be an abstract.
If we dont want to make that inherited class as abstract then we have to override the abstract method. 
note: we cannot create a object for abstract class. 

How yo create a abstract method?
Must be prefixed with the abstract keyword.
must end with the semicolon;
does not have a method body.


We cannot create static method as abstract method.

in abstarct class we can create static variable, non static , static methid , non sttaic methid, abstract methiod, static intislizer block , 
instance initializer block and constructor.
In abstarct class we can create abstract method  as well as non static concrete methods , hence we cannot acheive 100% abstrction using abstract class.
If we want to acheive 100% of abstraction then we have to use interface.


Interface :

Interface is a keyword it is used to create non primitive datatype.
It is used to acheive  100% of abstraction.
It is use to acheive multiple incheritance.

To inherit interface into class we use implements keyword.
with the help of implements keyword we can inherit more than one interface.
We cannot create object of interface.

IN Interface we cannot create static initializer block, instance intislizer block, constructor.

In interface all the non static methods already prefixed with abstract and public keyword, hence we can acheive 100% abstraction using interface.

In interface all the variables are already prefixed with final and static keyword.
If any variable is prefixed with final keyword which means we cannot re- initialize that variable

Static method of interface can be access only using static way.

Types of interfaces:
1.Regular or normal interfaces
2.Marker interface
3.Functional interface 
